1
00:00:00,084 --> 00:00:01,884
(Bernadette:)What kind of comics do the guys like?

2
00:00:02,052 --> 00:00:05,382
(Stuart:)Um, a little bit of everything.
Mostly superhero stuff.

3
00:00:05,589 --> 00:00:08,679
- All right, well, who's the best superhero?
- Shh!

4
00:00:08,859 --> 00:00:12,589
(Stuart:)You can't ask a question like that in here.
Are you trying to start a rumble?

5
00:00:14,198 --> 00:00:15,898
Well, what do you recommend?

6
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:19,300
(Stuart:)Well, uh, let's see, you've got your basic
clean-cut good guys:

7
00:00:19,503 --> 00:00:22,163
(Stuart:)Superman, Spider-Man, Captain America.

8
00:00:22,373 --> 00:00:24,343
Then you have your darker anti-heroes:

9
00:00:24,542 --> 00:00:26,572
(Stuart:)Your Batman, your Wolverine, Punisher.

10
00:00:26,811 --> 00:00:28,801
(Amy:)Ooh, I do love a bad boy.

11
00:00:30,815 --> 00:00:33,805
(Penny:)As evidenced by your boyfriend
and his fear of hamsters.

12
00:00:36,554 --> 00:00:38,714
(Sheldon:)If I were you,
I'd go for Fables number one.

13
00:00:38,923 --> 00:00:41,413
(Stuart:)Artwork is sophisticated,
it's intelligently written...

14
00:00:41,625 --> 00:00:43,025
(Stuart:)...and it doesn't objectify...

15
00:00:43,194 --> 00:00:46,094
(Stuart:)...or stereotype women.
- Oh, Thor. He's hot.

16
00:00:47,431 --> 00:00:49,631
(Stuart:)Yeah, he kind of is.

17
00:00:54,972 --> 00:00:56,442
(Raj:)And we're blending...

18
00:00:56,640 --> 00:01:04,020
(Raj:)...and we're blending, and we're done.

